{'symbol': 'CTRA', 'date': '2019-09-30 22:30:00', 'title': 'CONTURA ENERGY, INC. (NYSE:CTRA) CANCELLED THE ACQUISITION OF ALL ASSETS OF THE BELLE AYR, EAGLE BUTTE THERMAL COAL MINES AND S-7 SURFACE METALLURGICAL COAL MINE FROM BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C.', 'text': 'CONTURA ENERGY, INC. (NYSE:CTRA) AGREED TO ACQUIRE ALL ASSETS OF THE BELLE AYR, EAGLE BUTTE THERMAL COAL MINES AND S-7 SURFACE METALLURGICAL COAL MINE FROM BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C. FOR $20.6 MILLION ON JULY 24, 2019. CONTURA ENERGY WILL SERVE AS STALKING HORSE PURCHASER FOR THE ASSETS. CONTURA ENERGY, INC. (NYSE:CTRA) ENTERED INTO AN ASSET PURCHASE AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE ALL ASSETS OF THE BELLE AYR, EAGLE BUTTE THERMAL COAL MINES AND S-7 SURFACE METALLURGICAL COAL MINE FROM BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C. IN AUGUST 2019. IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE PROPOSED STALKING HORSE BID, CONTURA WOULD PROVIDE AN INITIAL PURCHASE DEPOSIT OF $8.1 MILLION. THE PURCHASE DEPOSIT IS EXPECTED TO BE USED TO FACILITATE AN ORDERLY ASSET SALE PROCESS, AS WELL AS COVER BLACKJEWEL’S NEAR-TERM WORKING CAPITAL NEEDS AND GENERAL CORPORATE EXPENSES.\xa0IF NO SUPERIOR BIDS ARE ACCEPTED, CONTURA WOULD PAY AN ADDITIONAL $12.5 MILLION IN CASH FOR THE ASSETS. CONTURA WOULD ACQUIRE SUBSTANTIALLY ALL OF THE ASSETS OF THE BELLE AYR AND EAGLE BUTTE THERMAL COAL MINES IN THE POWDER RIVER BASIN IN CAMPBELL COUNTY, WYOMING, INCLUDING RELATED FACILITIES AND EQUIPMENT, AS WELL AS SUBSTANTIALLY ALL OF THE ASSETS OF THE S-7 SURFACE METALLURGICAL COAL MINE, IN FAYETTE COUNTY, WEST VIRGINIA, INCLUDING RELATED FACILITIES AND EQUIPMENT. PURSUANT TO THE TERMS OF THE PROPOSED TRANSACTION, CONTURA WOULD ACQUIRE THE SPECIFIED ASSETS FREE AND CLEAR OF ALL LIENS, CLAIMS, INTERESTS AND ENCUMBRANCES, AND WOULD ASSUME NO LIABILITIES WITH THE EXCEPTION OF ALL RECLAMATION OBLIGATIONS UNDER APPLICABLE LAW OR PERMITS AND ANY OTHER LIABILITIES EXPRESSLY AGREED TO BY CONTURA.\xa0IF APPROVED, UPON A SUCCESSFUL CLOSING OF THE PURCHASE OF THE WESTERN ASSETS SPECIFICALLY, CONTURA WILL ENDEAVOR TO HIRE THE MAJORITY OF THE DISPLACED WYOMING EMPLOYEES ASSOCIATED WITH THE BELLE AYR AND EAGLE BUTTE MINES AND RESUME NORMAL MINING OPERATIONS AS SOON AS THE COMPANY OBTAINS THE NECESSARY LEGAL AND REGULATORY APPROVALS TO DO SO.\xa0THE TRANSACTION IS SUBJECT TO CUSTOMARY CONDITIONS, CERTAIN GOVERNMENTAL, REGULATORY APPROVALS AND COURT-APPROVED BIDDING PROCEDURES. AS OF JULY 6, 2019, JUDGE FRANK VOLK APPROVED THE TRANSACTION. THE TRANSACTION IS EXPECTED TO CLOSE ON AUGUST 5, 2019. ON AUGUST 28, THE TRANSACTION WAS APPROVED BY THE BANKRUPTCY COURT.\n\nWILLIAM L. TAYLOR OF DAVIS POLK & WARDWELL LLP ACTED AS LEGAL ADVISOR AND DUCERA PARTNERS LLC ACTED AS FINANCIAL ADVISOR TO CONTURA. JOE M. SUPPLE OF SUPPLE LAW OFFICE, PLLC ACTED AS LEGAL ADVISOR FOR BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C. STEPHEN D. LERNER, NAVA HAZAN AND TRAVIS A. MCROBERTS OF SQUIRE PATTON BOGGS (US) LLP ACTED AS LEGAL ADVISORS FOR BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C.\nCONTURA ENERGY, INC. (NYSE:CTRA) CANCELLED THE ACQUISITION OF ALL ASSETS OF THE BELLE AYR, EAGLE BUTTE THERMAL COAL MINES AND S-7 SURFACE METALLURGICAL COAL MINE FROM BLACKJEWEL L.L.C. AND BLACKJEWEL HOLDINGS, L.L.C. ON OCTOBER 1, 2019. IN LIGHT OF THE SEEMINGLY INSURMOUNTABLE CHALLENGES POSED BY THE SALE OF THE ASSETS TO CONTURA, BLACKJEWEL AND ITS ADVISORS, WITH CONTURA’S CONSENT, HAVE DETERMINED THAT IT IS IN THE BEST INTERESTS OF BLACKJEWEL, THEIR ESTATES AND THEIR CREDITORS TO INSTEAD SELL THE ASSETS TO EAGLE SPECIALTY MATERIALS IN A PRIVATE SALE WITHOUT ANY FURTHER SALE PROCESS OR AUCTION. \n'}